Myth: Before morning had a name, the world rested beneath a blue-black shell, and every creature moved by memory. Trees grew inward, rivers slept under stones, and people kept warm beside roots that glimmered like buried stars. Only Ila, a quiet child with a clay bowl, wondered what waited beyond the dark.

